In article <30453@ucbvax.BERKELEY.EDU> wisner@mica.Berkeley.EDU (Bill Wisner, Libertine) writes:
>Let's face it. Wizards are wimps. And the junky equipment they get stuck
>with doesn't help much. So why not stop giving them junky equipment?

I have to disagree with this sentiment.  IMHO the wizard character class is
one of the more challenging of the character classes.  This character class
requires the player to really think about what they have and how they can
use these things to their best advantage.  I'll admit that some of the
wizard characters I've created have been doomed from the start (I agree that
2 uncursed rings of aggravate monster is a real downer) but I have found that
most of my wizard characters have died due more to my ineptitude then to their
lack of equipment (acutally, I've died while eating far too many times 8-( ).
The person playing the wizard, like the character class, must have a high
intellegence if they hope to survive.
